The proposed plan is good and aligns with the overall architecture of the LMS. I approve the direction, but before implementation I want to improve several parts of the design so that the API Gateway follows enterprise microservice security practices.

Please update the implementation according to the following requirements before generating code.

===========================================================
GENERAL REQUIREMENTS
===========================================================

Analyze the complete api-gateway project before making any changes.

Do NOT regenerate the project.

Do NOT rewrite unrelated code.

Modify ONLY api-gateway.

Do NOT modify auth-service or any business microservice.

===========================================================
JWT LIBRARY
===========================================================

Use the latest stable JJWT version that is fully compatible with the Spring Boot version already used in the project.

Do not use an older version unless there is a compatibility requirement.

===========================================================
JWT VALIDATION
===========================================================

The Gateway must validate

• Signature

• Expiration

• Issuer

• Subject

• Authorities

• User ID

Do not trust any client supplied information.

===========================================================
HEADER SECURITY
===========================================================

This requirement is mandatory.

Before forwarding a request,

remove any incoming headers named

X-User-Id

X-User-Email

X-User-Role

X-User-Authorities

Clients must never be allowed to send these headers.

Only after successful JWT validation should the Gateway create and forward trusted headers.

===========================================================
FORWARDED USER CONTEXT
===========================================================

Forward the following headers to downstream services.

X-User-Id

X-User-Email

X-User-Role

X-User-Authorities

The values must come only from the validated JWT.

===========================================================
ROUTE SECURITY
===========================================================

Public routes

/api/v1/auth/register

/api/v1/auth/login

/swagger-ui/**

/v3/api-docs/**

/actuator/health

Everything else must require a valid JWT.

===========================================================
ERROR HANDLING
===========================================================

Return a consistent JSON response using the project's standard ApiResponse structure.

Handle

401 Unauthorized

403 Forbidden

Expired Token

Invalid Token

Malformed Token

Missing Token

Invalid Signature

===========================================================
FILTER IMPLEMENTATION
===========================================================

The AuthenticationFilter should be clean and lightweight.

Move all JWT parsing and validation logic into JwtUtil or a dedicated JwtService.

The filter should only

• Determine whether authentication is required.

• Validate the JWT.

• Remove spoofed headers.

• Add trusted headers.

• Continue the request.

===========================================================
CODE QUALITY
===========================================================

Follow

SOLID Principles

Single Responsibility Principle

Constructor Injection

Reusable Components

Meaningful Package Structure

Do not duplicate JWT validation logic.

===========================================================
DOCUMENTATION
===========================================================

Update

README.md

docs/security/api-gateway-jwt.md

Include

Gateway Security Architecture

JWT Validation Flow

Header Forwarding Strategy

Header Spoofing Prevention

Public vs Protected Routes

===========================================================
TESTING
===========================================================

Verify

✓ Register works without JWT

✓ Login works without JWT

✓ Protected APIs reject missing tokens

✓ Protected APIs reject expired tokens

✓ Protected APIs reject malformed tokens

✓ Protected APIs reject tampered tokens

✓ Valid JWT allows access

✓ Gateway removes spoofed headers

✓ Gateway forwards trusted headers correctly

✓ Existing routes continue to work

===========================================================
IMPORTANT
===========================================================

This Gateway should NOT perform authorization decisions based on business logic.

The Gateway is responsible only for

Authentication

JWT Validation

Trusted User Context Forwarding

Business authorization will remain inside the downstream microservices.

